    {
      "step": "Controlling principle",
      "finding": "The justification of killing in defense of others cannot rest on the private fear of a single actor, however well-founded that fear may be, when the realm retains institutions and means to remove a ruler through collective judgment, and when those means have not been exhausted. To permit it would be to subordinate law itself to the discretion of any person convinced of danger."
